# Cursor IDE Project Rules: Blood Donation Network (BDN)

# Tech Stack & Language Guidelines
- Always use TypeScript with strict mode enabled. Never introduce `any` types.
- Backend: Node.js 20 LTS, Express.js, Prisma ORM, Zod, PostgreSQL 16 with PostGIS.
- Frontend: Next.js 14+ (App Router), React 18, Tailwind CSS, TanStack Query.

# Architecture & Layer Boundaries
- Enforce strict 4-layer separation: Presentation -> Service -> Data -> Integration.
- Controllers parse HTTP inputs, validate via Zod, and delegate to Domain Services.
- Database access must occur through Prisma ORM or PostGIS `$queryRaw`.
- Domain logic (cooldown calculators, blood compatibility matrix) must be pure TypeScript.

# Security Guardrails
- Validate all API inputs using Zod.
- Hash passwords using Argon2id.
- Obfuscate donor identity (name/phone) from hospital view until match acceptance.
- Include audit log trigger (`AuditService.log()`) on all high-privilege operations.

# Documentation Synchronization
- If you add or modify a Prisma model, update `DATABASE.md`.
- If you add or modify a REST endpoint, update `API_SPEC.md`.
- If you alter RBAC roles or security middleware, update `SECURITY.md`.
